:: panwala_delivery_scene
You hand Guard Patil the Classic Milds packet through the booth window. He nods once, tucks it under the register, and   miracle   doesn't ask for your ID this time.

<div class="dialogue">"Bhau ko bol   hisaab kal."<span class="gloss-en">Tell Bhau   we'll settle up tomorrow.</span></div>

<<run setup.removeItem("panwala_packet")>>
<<run setup.flag("panwala_delivery_done")>>
<<run setup.addMoney(50, "arjun")>>
<<hubreturn>>


:: fruit_vendor_npc
Tai runs the cart where Katraj Road meets the PG lane   pomegranates, guavas, a pyramid of sitaphal. Nine-yard saree, several gold teeth.

<div class="dialogue">"Arjun! Kela le ja."<span class="gloss-en">Arjun! Take a banana.</span></div>

"Tai, mera pet bhi khali hai aur wallet bhi."<span class="gloss-en">Tai, my stomach's empty and so is my wallet.</span>

She tsks   the Maharashtrian tsk that carries volumes. Thrusts two bananas at you. "Free. Amma ko bolna   unka ladka kha nahi raha."<span class="gloss-en">Free. Tell your mother   her boy isn't eating.</span> Then, because your emotional state is visible from space: "Ladki theek hai teri? Hum sab jaante hain, beta. Katraj mein kuch chhupta nahi."<span class="gloss-en">Is your girl okay? We all know, son. Nothing stays hidden in Katraj.</span>

<<run setup.stat("energy", 2, "arjun")>>
<<hubreturn>>


:: stray_dog_scene
<<if not setup.hasItem("biscuit")>>\
The brown dog checks your hands, finds them empty, and gives you a look of profound disappointment. You'd need biscuits   the tapri sells Parle-G.
<<hubreturn>>
<<elseif setup.has("dog_fed")>>\
The dog trots over, leans its bony flank against your knee for a while, and accepts another biscuit as its due.
<<hubreturn>>
<<else>>\
You crouch and break the Parle-G into pieces. He approaches low to the ground   food first, human second   and takes each piece gently, like a surgeon removing a suture. Then he sits beside you, leaning his weight into your leg. For about thirty seconds you have something that loves you without conditions or surveillance.

"Tujhe bhi koi mil jaaye, bhai,"<span class="gloss-en">May you find someone too, brother,</span> you tell him. He wags.

<<run setup.flag("dog_fed")>>
<<hubreturn>>
<</if>>


:: ananya_library_scene
<<img "ananya_library.png" "Ananya, library table">>
<<if setup.has("ananya_conversation_done")>>\
Ananya lifts her earphone. "Still can't believe I stared at that bug for two days." She goes back to her pathfinding visualiser, nodes blooming across the screen.
<<hubreturn>>
<<else>>\
Two desks over   Ananya, 2nd-year CSE, ponytail, VS Code open, typing like she's debugging production at 3 AM. She glances at you. Away. Back.

<div class="dialogue">"Arjun, right? You wrote that sorting visualiser Krishnan showed in class. The recursive partitioning animation was elegant."</div>

She turns her laptop toward you   a pathfinding visualiser, an A-star bug she can't find. It takes you forty-five seconds. "Line 87. Your heuristic is Manhattan distance but your grid allows diagonal movement. You need Chebyshev, or it over-explores."

She fixes it, runs it, grins the grin of a coder whose code just worked. Then, carefully: "Random question. You know B.J. Medical, Sassoon Road? My cousin's third-year MBBS there. Sneha Patil. Room 302. She says the library has a rare Sanskrit section   I'm into computational linguistics, thought I could get some corpora."

The world contracts. Room 302. The room next to Room 304. The room next to Meera.

"I might be able to help," you say carefully. "Let me check with some people."

<<run setup.flag("ananya_conversation_done")>>
<<run setup.flag("ananya_has_bj_connection")>>
<<hubreturn>>
<</if>>


:: sinhagad_dhaba_scene
The dhaba is halfway up the approach road   tin roof, four plastic tables, a kerosene stove, and all of Pune laid out below. The owner is seventy, white stubble, a cloth wrapped round his head.

<div class="dialogue">"Chai?" One word. He makes it on the kerosene flame, unhurried. "Pehle dost ke saath aata tha. Aur ek ladki bhi thi   lambe baal, sundar. Ab akela hai."<span class="gloss-en">You used to come with a friend. And there was a girl too   long hair, pretty. Now you're alone.</span></div>

He remembers. This man, this dhaba, this mountain   they remember Meera and you.

"Woh nahi aa sakti abhi."<span class="gloss-en">She can't come right now.</span>

He nods. Doesn't ask why. "Chai pi. Sab theek hoga."<span class="gloss-en">Drink your tea. Everything will be alright.</span> Turns back to his stove. That's the whole philosophy.

<<if not setup.hasItem("night_ride_invitation")>>\
On your way out, three Royal Enfield boys rumble up. "Night ride kal   Sinhagad Fort, midnight, fifteen bikes. Girls bhi aa rahi hain. Soch le."<span class="gloss-en">Night ride tomorrow   Sinhagad Fort, midnight, fifteen bikes. Girls are coming too. Think about it.</span> One scrawls a number on a Classic Milds wrapper and drops it on the table.
<<run setup.addItem("night_ride_invitation")>>
<</if>>

<<run setup.stat("energy", 3, "arjun")>>
<<hubreturn>>


:: ice_cream_vendor_npc
The ice cream wala's cart plays a tinny loop of a film song. You get an orange bar. It's mostly ice and a rumour of orange, and for a few minutes on the lakeside bench that is exactly enough.

<<hubreturn>>


:: sunita_interaction
Aai is in the kitchen, which is where Aai is. "Beta, kha liya? Sirf dosa? Dosa mein kya hota hai   maida aur aloo."<span class="gloss-en">Son, have you eaten? Just a dosa? What's in a dosa   refined flour and potato.</span> She's already ladling something onto a plate you didn't ask for. "Sunday aa. Pooja ko maths samjha. Main mutton le lungi."<span class="gloss-en">Come Sunday. Teach Pooja maths. I'll get mutton.</span>

The invitation is a command wrapped in love wrapped in calories. You say //dekhta hoon//.<span class="gloss-en">I'll see.</span> She hears //yes//.

<<run setup.stat("energy", 4, "arjun")>>
<<hubreturn>>


:: suresh_interaction
Papa lowers the newspaper. "Placement season aa raha hai. Resume ready hai? LIC mein bhi opening hai, back-office   permanent, pension."<span class="gloss-en">Placement season is coming. Is your resume ready? There's an opening at LIC too, back-office   permanent, pension.</span> He means well. He measures a life in permanence and pension and cannot understand why that isn't comforting.

"Dekhta hoon, Papa."<span class="gloss-en">I'll see, Papa.</span>

<<hubreturn>>


:: pooja_interaction
Pooja is on the sofa, textbooks unopened, phone very open. "Bhaiya WiFi password   SunitaAai2024, capital S, I know, it's cringe, Papa set it."<span class="gloss-en">Brother, WiFi password  </span> Then, without looking up: "Meera bhabhi ka update?<span class="gloss-en">Any update on Meera bhabhi (sister-in-law)?</span> ...Sorry. That was mean. Love you bhaiya. Come Sunday, Aai's making mutton."

Seventeen years old and already more emotionally perceptive than most adults you know.

<<hubreturn>>


:: rohit_cad_scene
<<if setup.has("rohit_cad_fixed")>>\
Rohit's piston render sits on the screen, smooth and correct. He shows it to everyone who enters the room. "Mera project. Genius, na?"<span class="gloss-en">My project. Genius, right?</span>
<<hubreturn>>
<<else>>\
Rohit's laptop shows SolidWorks and a 3D model that might be a piston or might be modern art. He hits render. The screen goes black, then white, then an error message in the specific red software uses when it's personally insulted.

"Rohit, tera mesh density itni high hai ki render engine ko anxiety ho raha hai."<span class="gloss-en">Rohit, your mesh density is so high the render engine is having anxiety.</span>

"Mesh density kya hota hai?"<span class="gloss-en">What's mesh density?</span>

Twenty minutes later you've optimised the mesh, fixed two dimensions that would have made his piston the size of a building, and corrected a material assignment that gave steel the transparency of glass. The render completes   silver, gleaming.

He's quiet a moment. Then: "Aaj canteen mein jo bola   usse related. Ek junior tha, Sameer, second year. Usne B.J. Medical ki library mein ek ladki dekhi. Lambe baal, fair, braid. Kisi ne bola woh Kulkarni hai. Colonel Kulkarni ki ladki. Parso. Sanskrit type ka kuch padh rahi thi."<span class="gloss-en">What I said in the canteen today   related to that. There was a junior, Sameer, second year. He saw a girl in the B.J. Medical library. Long hair, fair, in a braid. Someone said she's a Kulkarni. Colonel Kulkarni's daughter. Day before yesterday. Reading some Sanskrit-type thing.</span>

Your hands stop on the keyboard. Meera. In the library. Reading Sanskrit. Two days ago. Alive. Functioning. In a place you can almost reach.

"Rohit. Thanks."

"Chal, biryani order kar. Tera Swiggy   mere pe coupon nahi hai."<span class="gloss-en">Come on, order biryani. On your Swiggy   I don't have a coupon.</span>

<<run setup.flag("rohit_cad_fixed")>>
<<run setup.flag("rohit_reveals_meera_sighting")>>
<<hubreturn>>
<</if>>
